course: dictionary
lesson: 13250
title: Ghostly: spooky and faint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Ghostly» is an adjective, a describing word. It comes from «ghost», so it means like a ghost, or to do with ghosts. «The ghostly figure drifted across the dark garden.» The words dark and drifted tell you the figure is strange and spooky.
explain: Ghostly can also mean faint and hard to see or hear, as if it is not quite real. «A ghostly shape loomed in the thick fog.» You cannot see the shape clearly, so ghostly means faint and blurry here. Ask yourself: does the sentence feel spooky, or faint? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Writers choose ghostly to build a creepy mood. «Her face looked ghostly pale in the moonlight.» Pale and ghostly together make the reader picture someone very white and frightening. Look at the other words in the sentence to decide which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Ghostly is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a ghostly figure, a ghostly whisper.
fact: «Ghostly» means like a ghost, or to do with ghosts: pale, faint and strange.
fact: «Ghostly» can also mean faint and hard to see or hear, as if not quite real.
fact: The comparative forms are ghostlier (more ghostly) and ghostliest (most ghostly).
fact: Writers often use ghostly for mist, moonlight and echoes to make a story feel spooky.
exercise: «The ghostly figure drifted across the dark garden.» What does ghostly mean here? | Made of wood | Very hungry | *Like a ghost, pale and strange | Loud and cheerful
exercise: «A ghostly shape loomed in the thick fog.» What does ghostly suggest here? | Bright and golden | *Faint and hard to see, as if not quite real | Very loud and cheerful | Hungry and tired
exercise: Why might a writer choose ghostly for a spooky story? | *It builds a creepy, spooky mood | It is the name of a town | It means exactly the same as happy | It means very fast
test: «The ghostly echo faded slowly in the empty hall.» What does ghostly mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Very hungry | *Faint and hard to hear, as if not quite real | Made of wood
test: «The moonlight made the old house look ghostly.» What is the best meaning here? | Wet and muddy | Hot and sticky | Bright and cheerful, like a sunny day | *Like a ghost, pale and spooky
exam: Which word means more ghostly? | ghostly | ghostliness | *ghostlier | ghostlessly
